{“verdict”:”NO - BEHAVIOR CHANGE”,”explanation”:”In CODE1, B.k() has no parameters and B.k(int a) is inherited from A returning 1, so B.test() calling k(2) dispatches to A.k(int) returning 1. In CODE2, B.k(int a) overrides A.k(int a) returning 2, so B.test() calling k(2) now dispatches to B.k(int a) returning 2. The observable return value of test() changes from 1 to 2.”,”junit_test”:”import org.junit.Test;\nimport static org.junit.Assert.assertEquals;\n\npublic class BehaviorTest {\n @Test\n public void testKDispatch() {\n B b = new B();\n assertEquals(1L, b.test());\n }\n}”}